Z||000008||william_thorniii||03-17-2000||03:32 PM||||Lar,<P>That reminds me of a story that my buddy told me one time.  I let him drive my 87 CP in stead of his truck from Flint to Greenville so he could save a little gas $.  <P>He has a multitude of little cousins running around down there.  He told me that when he was packing the trunk that he sat two of them on the ledges of the trunk (flat spots inside the trunk to the extreme L & R hand sides).  He claimed that they loved it and wouldn't get out on their own.<P>He does come from a crazy family though.  When growing up, he had a pet... a water buffalo!  He is from the extreme Southern tip of India in case any of you are wondering.  I guess having a water buffalo down there isn't nearly as strange as it would be if you lived in Ohio.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
